UID:10003268-1793125800-1793133000@www.culturelink.ca
SUMMARY:Invisible Suitcase
DESCRIPTION:An art workshop about home\, memories and your new life in Canada.\nFor Spanish-speaking newcomers. \nMoving to a new country means bringing more than what fits in a suitcase. \nThrough a fun and creative art activity\, create your own “invisible suitcase” and explore the memories\, traditions\, people\, dreams\, and pieces of home that you carry with you. \nWho can participate: newcomer who are Permanent Residents or Convention Refugees\, and at least 18 years old. \nThis Activity will be in Spanish\, with guest speaker: Paola Gomez\, Co-Founder & Program Director at MUSE Arts Toronto. \nTo register\, fill out this FORM. \nFor more information\, email Marina at msokolov@culturelink.ca.
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/invisible-suitcase/
LOCATION:CultureLink\, 2340 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6P\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Newcomer-Wellness-Program-Web-Icon.png
END:VEVENT
